Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit
MIME-Version: 1.0

Team,

A reminder of our desk policy, which applies to every book we run, the client books included:

Any order, buy or sell, that is large against the stock's recent liquidity - above the threshold set for the book, measured as a percentage of the stock's average daily volume over its last 20 trading sessions, in today's shares - needs my approval before it goes to the market. That includes sells we have to make, for instance to close out a stock compliance has restricted.

The percentage is set per book; ask me if you do not have it for the book you work on. If you need an exception, write to me in advance with the order and the reason.

Desk head
